SIM-02: treat TEMPCLOSED GPVs and PBVs as closed

tankstatus() marks a valve that would drain an empty tank (or fill a
full one) TEMPCLOSED. gpvcoeff() only tested for CLOSED, and the active
branch of pbvcoeff() never looked at the status, so both valves kept
passing flow that newlinkflows() did not charge to the tank. Test
<= CLOSED in both, as pipecoeff(), pumpcoeff() and valvecoeff() do.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-02_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydcoeffs.c b/src/hydcoeffs.c
index d0b03c2..78a39d4 100644
--- a/src/hydcoeffs.c
+++ b/src/hydcoeffs.c
@@ -966,7 +966,7 @@ void  gpvcoeff(Project *pr, int k)
     Hydraul *hyd = &pr->hydraul;
 
     // Treat as a pipe if valve closed
-    if (hyd->LinkStatus[k] == CLOSED) valvecoeff(pr, k);
+    if (hyd->LinkStatus[k] <= CLOSED) valvecoeff(pr, k);
 
     // Otherwise utilize segment of head loss curve
     // bracketing current flow (curve index is stored
@@ -1003,8 +1003,9 @@ void  pbvcoeff(Project *pr, int k)
     Hydraul *hyd = &pr->hydraul;
     Slink *link = &pr->network.Link[k];
 
-    // If valve fixed OPEN or CLOSED then treat as a pipe
-    if (hyd->LinkSetting[k] == MISSING || hyd->LinkSetting[k] == 0.0)
+    // If valve closed, or fixed OPEN or CLOSED, then treat as a pipe
+    if (hyd->LinkStatus[k] <= CLOSED ||
+        hyd->LinkSetting[k] == MISSING || hyd->LinkSetting[k] == 0.0)
     {
         valvecoeff(pr, k);
     }
